<report>
<line><title>Probit analysis - <in>title</in></title></line>
<line>constant = <in>a</in></line>
<line>slope = <in>b</in></line>
<line></line>
<line>Median * Dose = <in>mxd</in></line>
<line><warn>Confidence interval <in>het</in> = <in>from</in> to <in>to</in></warn></line>
<line></line>
<line>* Dose for centile <in>centile</in> = <in>doseq</in></line>
<line><warn>Confidence interval <in>het_cent</in> = <in>from_cent</in> to <in>to_cent</in></warn></line>
<line></line>
<line>Chi&#xb2; (heterogeneity of deviations from model) = <in>dev</in>  (<in>df</in> df)  <in>p</in></line>
<line></line>
<line>t for slope = <in>t_slope</in> (<in>df</in> df_slope)  <in>p_slope</in><block name="warn"></line>
<line><pval>WARNING: slope not significant</pval></block></line>
<line></line>
<line></line>
</report>
